INSERT INTO corpus VALUES(2151,'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1188401','The dimensional approach to clinical psychopharmacology: a polysemous concept.','Baruch P, Filteau MJ, Bouchard RH, Pourcher E, Vincent P, Jouvent R.','1992','psychotropes psychotropes psychopathologies asberg traskman thoren hiaa ashcroft eccleston sharman macdougall binns hydroxyindole azmitia azmitia banki arato kurcz ballenger goyer cloninger eison anxiolytics jouvent fiszbein opler panss linnoila virkkunen scheinin nuutila rimon hydroxyindoleacetic nonimpulsive ninan kammen scheinin linnoila bunney hydroxyindoleacetic schizophrenic peroutka sleight hekmatpanah jnp praag lakke jpwf schut depressions s0033291700056385 siever psychobiological stelmack praagh leijnse neubewertung syndroms skizze funktionellen widlocher praag praag asnis wetzler bleich korn denosologization','Abstract The last decade has seen significant progress in the development and specific clinical application of selective psychotropes. The dimensional approach to clinical psychopharmacology views the behavioral targets of psychotropes as phenomena existing on a continuum and as components, in varying degrees, of most psychopathologies. The modern concept of dimension has been used in different contexts. In psychology it has a mathematical sense, whereas in biological psychiatry it is associated more with biological function. This paper reviews these two concepts and the recent models attempting to merge them into one. The heuristic value of the dimensional approach, as well as some of its pitfalls and new avenues of research, are discussed. Full text PDF Previous 55 56 57 58 59 60 Next Selected References These references are in PubMed. This may not be the complete list of references from this article. Andreasen N. C., Olsen S. Negative v positive schizophrenia. Definition and validation. Arch Gen Psychiatry. 1982 Jul;39(7):789–794. doi: 10.1001/archpsyc.1982.04290070025006. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ]