. 2009;6:84–88. [ Google Scholar ] 33. Hodges BD, Kuper A. Theory and practice in the design and conduct of graduate medical education. Acad Med. 2012;87:25–33. doi: 10.1097/ACM.0b013e318238e069. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 34. Nawka A, Kuzman MR, Giacco D, et al. Mental health reforms in Europe: challenges of postgraduate psychiatric training in Europe: a trainee perspective. Psychiatric Serv. 2010;61(9):862–864. doi: 10.1176/ps.2010.61.9.862. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 35. Hatch JM, Cunliffe AL (2013) Organization theory: modern, symbolic and postmodern perspectives. Oxford University Press, pp 260–265 36. Lasagna L (1964) “Hippocratic Oath—Modern Version”. WGBH Educational Foundation 37. Pinto da Costa M, Guerra C, Malta R, et al. Psychiatry training towards a global future: trainees’ perspective in Portugal. Acta Med Port. 2013;26:357–360. [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 38. Pinto da Costa M (2012) A challenge of the 21st century: brain migration in psychiatry. Int Psychiatry 9(3):75–76. http://www.epha.org/IMG/pdf/Letter_IntPsychiatry_EFPT_Brain_migration.pdf 39. Fiorillo A, Del Vecchio V, Luciano M, Sampogna G, Beezhold J. This is why there is hope for psychiatry. World Psychiatry. 2014;1:98–99. doi: 10.1002/wps.20110. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 40. Fiorillo A, Luciano M, Giacco D, et al. Training and practice of psychotherapy in Europe: results of a survey. World Psychiatry. 2011;10:238. doi: 10.1002/j.2051-5545.2011.tb00064.x. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 41. Fiorillo A, Malik A, Luciano M, Del Vecchio V, Sampogna G, Del Gaudio L, et al. Challenges for trainees in psychiatry and early career psychiatrists. Int Rev Psychiatry. 2013;25:431–437. doi: 10.3109/09540261.2013.812960. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 42. Riese F, Oakley C, Bendix M, Piir P, Fiorillo A. Transition from psychiatric training to independent practice: a survey on the situation of early career psychiatri